1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Chapter 1: Quick Add. Add many items fast: take photos, review them, name them,
save them. You need: a few items to photograph, and about 5 minutes. Quick Add
is ordinary photo capture. Naming and details are typed by you. AI
identification is a separate, optional button, and it is not on every account.

2
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:36,875
Step 1. Start on Home. On Home, the Quick Add and ADD ITEM buttons sit side by
side in the top card.

3
00:00:36,875 --> 00:00:51,500
Step 2. The same buttons are in your Vault. In the Vault they are at the top
right. A new Vault also shows Quick Add and Add manually in the middle.

4
00:00:51,500 --> 00:01:11,625
Step 3. A new, empty Vault offers four starting points. Scan your first item
opens the Add Item form. Quick Add opens the multi-photo camera. Add manually
opens a simpler typing-only form. Import brings in a spreadsheet.

5
00:01:11,625 --> 00:01:32,500
Step 4. Upload from device offers two routes. Upload from device asks: Single
item (all the photos go on one item, in Add Item) or Batch (each photo becomes a
new item, in Bulk Upload). Bulk Upload is not covered in this tutorial.

6
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:55,000
Step 5. Add manually is a different, typing-only form. Add manually opens a
separate one-page form. Its required field is called Title, and it has its own
photo area and extra fields. This tutorial teaches the main Add Item form and
Quick Add instead.

7
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:19,000
Before the camera opens: Allow the camera. The first time, your browser asks to
use the camera. Choose Allow. On a phone it may say While using the app. If you
choose Block, Quick Add tells you so. Next, we show that message. Photos stay on
your device until you save them to your Vault.

8
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:31,750
Step 6. Quick Add opens the camera. Quick Add is a full-screen camera. Take as
many photos as you like, then press Finished. (Simulated: The picture in the
viewfinder comes from a test camera that plays a synthetic, fictional card
picture. The real camera permission prompt is drawn by the browser and cannot be
captured.)

9
00:02:31,750 --> 00:02:53,625
Step 7. If the camera is blocked. If you tapped Block, Quick Add says: Camera
access is blocked for this site. Allow the camera in your browser's site
settings, then reopen Quick Add. Without a camera you can still use Upload or
Add manually. (Simulated: The permission was set to Blocked in the test browser;
the message is the app's own.)

10
00:02:53,625 --> 00:03:08,625
Step 8. Optionally pick a Universe first. Choose a Universe before you shoot so
new photos start in the right place. You can still change each one later.

11
00:03:08,625 --> 00:03:17,500
Step 9. ...and a Category. Category narrows it further, for example Cards.

12
00:03:17,500 --> 00:03:32,625
Step 10. Press the round button to take a photo. Press the round shutter button.
The counter in the corner goes up and the newest photo appears bottom left.
(Simulated: Test camera picture (synthetic, fictional card).)

13
00:03:32,625 --> 00:03:47,875
Step 11. Keep going: one photo per item. Four photos so far. One of them was an
accident, and we will remove it in a moment. Press Finished when you are done.
(Simulated: Test camera pictures (synthetic, fictional items).)

14
00:03:47,875 --> 00:03:58,875
Step 12. Review what you captured. Every photo is listed. Spot the accidental
one? Press Remove on it.

15
00:03:58,875 --> 00:04:18,125
Step 13. The unwanted photo is gone. Three items remain. The removed photo shows
Undo, in case you change your mind. Each item has its own Universe and Category
you can correct. Then press Add 3 items to Vault.

16
00:04:18,125 --> 00:04:36,250
Step 14. Correct a detail before saving. Item 3 is a toy, but Pop Culture
started on Comics. Change its Category to Toys & Figures. Every item's Universe
and Category can be corrected like this.

17
00:04:36,250 --> 00:04:48,875
Step 15. Name each item. Type a name for each item. Universe, Category, Cost and
Value are optional and can be added later.

18
00:04:48,875 --> 00:05:02,125
Step 16. Add what you know. Cost is what you paid. Leave Cost or Value empty
when you do not know it: empty means unknown, not zero.

19
00:05:02,125 --> 00:05:22,500
Step 17. Identify with AI is optional and account-dependent. Nothing is
identified unless you press Identify with AI. AI is not on every account. If
yours does not have it, you see a message and fill the details in yourself.
(Simulated: This is the real answer from the live server for a test account that
does not have AI access. No AI request was paid for.)

20
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:35,875
Step 18. Saved: you land in your Vault. A message confirms the save and you are
back in your Vault, where all three items now appear.

21
00:05:35,875 --> 00:05:51,125
Step 19. Your new items are in the Vault. Scroll down in the Vault. Each new
item shows its photo and name. The chips above the list count items by Universe.

22
00:05:51,125 --> 00:06:02,125
Step 20. Search for an item by name. Type part of the name into the Vault search
box to find it again.

23
00:06:02,125 --> 00:06:13,250
Step 21. Open the item to check it. Open an item to see its photo and details
exactly as you saved them.

24
00:06:13,250 --> 00:06:39,250
Phone differences: Quick Add on a phone. The steps are the same. The layout
changes. Quick Add and ADD ITEM sit in a bar near the bottom of Home and the
Vault. The tab bar stays at the bottom: Home, Vault, Exhibitions, Lounge,
Discover. Sheets are taller and the buttons are bigger, so scroll inside a sheet
to see every item.

25
00:06:39,250 --> 00:06:58,750
Step 22. On a phone, the buttons sit at the bottom. On a phone, Quick Add and
ADD ITEM are in a bar near the bottom of Home and the Vault. The tab bar
underneath has Home, Vault, Exhibitions, Lounge and Discover.

26
00:06:58,750 --> 00:07:12,875
Step 23. Quick Add opens the camera. Quick Add fills the screen with the camera.
The round button takes a photo. Finished is at the top right. (Simulated: The
viewfinder shows a test camera playing a synthetic, fictional picture. On a real
phone the browser asks to allow the camera first; that prompt cannot be
captured.)

27
00:07:12,875 --> 00:07:27,375
Step 24. Take one photo per item. The counter shows how many photos you have.
Tap the small picture at the bottom left, or Finished, to review them.
(Simulated: The viewfinder shows a test camera playing a synthetic, fictional
picture. On a real phone the browser asks to allow the camera first; that prompt
cannot be captured.)

28
00:07:27,375 --> 00:07:40,875
Step 25. Remove the photo you do not want. Every photo is listed with its own
Universe and Category. Tap Remove on the accidental one.

29
00:07:40,875 --> 00:07:57,750
Step 26. Name each item, then save. Type a name for each item. Cost and Value
are optional. Identify with AI is optional and not on every account. Then tap
Save 3 items to Vault.

30
00:07:57,750 --> 00:08:08,000
Step 27. Back in your Vault. You land in your Vault. Scroll down to see your
three new items.

31
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:32,625
Chapter 1 recap: You used Quick Add. Open Quick Add from Home or the Vault. Take
one photo per item, then press Finished. Remove unwanted photos, correct
Universe and Category, type names. Save. Find your items in the Vault. Open one
to check it. Next: Chapter 2, the full Add Item form.
